# Upload list for `gcloud builds submit` (cloudbuild.yaml).
#
# CRITICAL: without this file, gcloud derives its ignore list from .gitignore, which
# excludes the model weights (engine/data/*.pt, *.npz, qwen_lora/) — the built image
# would then fail at container start. This file keeps engine/ (weights included) in the
# upload and trims everything the Docker build doesn't need, mirroring .dockerignore.
.git
.github
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.venv/
.venv*/
venv/
.idea/
.vscode/
.terraform/
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
service-account*.json
*credentials*.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
engine/data/*.previous
docs/
infra/
training/
web/
# The engine image COPYs only engine/ + regress/ (+ tests/ for the orchestrator build); everything
# below is build-irrelevant and was silently bloating the upload (spider caches/DBs alone were ~1.3 GB).
spider/
.model_taxbak/
scratch/
*.tar.gz
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
# NOTE: tests/ is intentionally NOT ignored — the orchestrator build (cloudbuild.orchestrator.yaml) runs
# tests.test_mcp / tests.test_orchestrator from the upload. It is not copied into the engine image
# (the engine Dockerfile COPYs only engine/), so keeping it costs a tiny upload and nothing in the image.
